Awakening kids  by letting them know that kidnapping  kids and being violent is wrong and  again the level of catharsis I felt  watching Reagan just completely owned  this entire organization with his words  and confidence alone Rivals the feeling  of watching mob one shot someone and  once Reagan reaches where mob is being  held he quickly dismisses all the grunts  by explaining to them that what they are  doing is actually a crime and they're  off on their merry way what's that you  say I've only been talking about Reagan  for the last three minutes correct  what's your point in seriousness though  the back half of this episode is somehow  even more remarkable than the first as  Reagan and MOB finally run into their  remaining claw scars Spirit Pokemon  trainer NAPA NAPA Samurai businessman  and Tiny gas mask girl who is the leader  of claw's seventh division somehow and  so Begins the true central conflict of  the rest of the season in a show sojam  packed with action comedy wonderful bits  of Animation every single element that  can be going for a show like this the  true conflict of this final mini Arc  isn't a big cinematic fight it isn't mob  hitting 100 and destroying everything in  his path rather it is Reagan wanting to  make sure that mob knows using powers  against others is wrong with four  separate scars directly threatening the  lives of his mentor family and friends  mob is so desperately backed into the  corner of being an anime protagonist and  fighting back but despite all of that  Reagan continues to insist that mob  shouldn't I find this core emotional  conflict so enthralling and not at all  what I expected going into this show we  all know that Mob Could wipe all four of  these people off the face of the Earth  without so much as a second thought but  should he he's just a kid a literal  middle schooler who hasn't even figured  out how to get his Crush to notice him  so often when we sit and watch shows  like this I think we tend to Discount  the reality of the situation  rationalizing it away as being necessary  or what other choice do they have but  Reagan rejects that entirely he walks  into this Arc Uninvited looks all  straight in the face and says are you  crazy these are kids and the hardest  part is it's difficult to say what is  right at this point because yes mob is  just a kid but he's a kid who is about  to be brutally murdered along with  everyone he knows if he doesn't fight  back does not hurting others with your  powers really weren't letting that  happen it's all happening so fast how is  Mob supposed to figure this out well  Reagan doesn't really give him a chance  to figure it out while everyone is  distracted trying to take mob out Reagan  whips out another one of his special  techniques this time in the form of a  simple drop kick to the leader ishiguru  and punching muraki in the face which  actually works surprisingly well at  least for long enough to let him talk  some more but unfortunately Lee Reagan  miscalculated here his plan to knock  some sense into these adults and take  them out of murdering actual children  means nothing when he's up against these  people they aren't really adults they're  practically grown children stuck in  Arrested Development still fighting  their battles and aiming for their goals  with fists and Blades so with all of  them completely ignoring Reagan's words  the big battle of the season commences  and wow what a battle this is this  entire show is incredibly animated but  perhaps nowhere is that as a parent as  these final fights in fact by the time  this episode was airing the entire anime  had wrapped up its production and  completed now that might not sound like  all that much of a feat since there's  only one episode left but unfortunately  almost all anime are run on a painfully  tight schedule so the fact that this  anime managed to wrap up production  entirely before its penultimate episode  even airs is remarkable to me this  episode also marks the entrance of what  a mob psycho 100's most prolific names  in its production hakuyu go tackling  multiple long cuts in both of the major  fights here he was 24 years of age when  this was made and had only just joined  the industry two years prior I mean how  do you even begin to talk about  something like that the background  animation the effects work and the  nakamura-esque inspired full drawn  environment I mean it's just absurd 24  years old let me remind you and while I  haven't watched it yet it is my  understanding that he is here to stay  going forward with mob psycho as an  absolute Powerhouse of a contributor to  this production as the fights continue  to progress Teru ritsu and Reagan  continue to lose ground and become more  in danger as tarot continues to call out  mob begging him to fight back for real  to save them all insurmountable pressure  then starts to build with each blow  traded in the background mob stress and  conviction grows further if he doesn't  do something they're all going to die  Reagan desperately pleads to mob to not  fight back  but they can't run they're all fending  off deadly attacks from powerful  psychics Reagan pleads one last time  don't fight against someone with  murderous intent  from all of this with nowhere else to  turn no choices left to make mob is  backed into a corner and as Mio sato's  absolutely remarkable painting glass  animation returns once again mob makes  his choice  oh  foreign  this moment is genuinely for me the  climax of the entire season the hard  caught from the build up of the music  and visuals surrounding mob's rage and  acceptance of murderous attempt to  Reagan smack him in the face and setting  him straight is absolutely Flawless  every single element presented to us  indicates that we were about to see mob  completely cut loose and showcase all of  his powers to us in a fantastic  demonstration of raw power and rage I  mean it's nearing the climax of the  anime of course it will and there's  plenty of Precedence set for this to  create our anticipation but with one  slap from Reagan every single element of  this anticipation is hard cut away from  in a single frame Reagan has managed to  cut through all of this and get it  through to mob and us as an audience and  later the rest of the people in the room  that this is all meaningless violence  and not how children should act the  entire scene is so incredibly subversive  of what you would expect from an anime  and the audio and visuals execute on  that completely flawlessly what a show  it is such a shock beautiful piece of  television and it couldn't have  concluded any other way really every  single action in this entire season  every character conflict surrounding mob  every piece of Reagan wackiness it all  comes collapsing in on a singular moment  and the flashback that follows we see  the very first time that mob beats  Reagan and Reagan plainly lays out the  central thesis of this entire season  just because you have psychic powers  doesn't make you any less human the same  goes for people who can run fast or are  smart or even who stink we all have  characteristics that define us and in  the end they are not what Define us what  matters is embracing who you are being  kind to others and becoming a good  person what a powerful theme what an  incredible message not just for the  child in distress here but for all of us  sizzle  foreign  much to my surprise the beginning of the  final episode doesn't begin with a giant  mob explosion but rather a quiet  realization that mob doesn't have to  fight that running is also an option at  which point Reagan leaps up from the  ground scolding The Swordsman for trying  to hurt him with a toy sword  um what well as we quickly begin to  realize it would appear in the stress  and emotional release of the moment  prior mob inadvertently projected his  100 or should I say one thousand percent  power into Reagan in sort of a flight or  flight response and boy oh boy does  Reagan put it to good use what follows  is a highly entertaining sequence of  Reagan Shenanigans completely  dismantling the psyches and beliefs of  these scars this power trip is so fun to  watch and at this point Reagan may as  well be the main character and once  again he manages to utterly Blindside Me  by putting into perspective what is  actually happening here these people  that think that they're special capable  of ruling the world with their strength  but they're not everyone is good at  something being a strong psychic isn't  going to make them popular hurting  others isn't going to fix Sakurai the  swordsman's traumatic childhood of dead  parents and Foster home abuse in fact as  Reagan describes he too had a tragic  childhood  one time he was young he forgot to tell  his parents that it was sports day at  school so he didn't have anything to eat  for lunch that particular day  foreign  despite the insanity of all of this  Reagan seems to manage to convince all  of the claws though it was mob's power  that facilitated his actions it was  actually his approach in Charisma that  made the difference all but their leader  ishiguro who as it turns out is oh dear  God he's a wrinkly old man make it go  away with Reagan's Powers run out and  MOB exhausted ishiguro's final tantrum  which surely spelled Doom for them all  if it wasn't for the fact the climax  happened last episode that is so as it  happens show that intern kid from a few  episodes back is actually the claws  Leader's kid and was checking up on the  seventh division the entire time  promptly putting an end to ishiguro and  caps off the combat disappointed however  in mob's decision to run the rest of  this episode is a sequence of really  cozy tie-ops and check-ins on all of her  characters mob is glad to be back at  school with his crushed the gym Bros  continue to be sick as all hell and Taro  is ready to lead the Awakening lab kids  onto higher highs Reagan able to see  dimple now is happy to have another  helper at his side and looming over the  distance claws leader seems to approach  if it isn't clear already I think this  resolution this Arc and well really this  whole season are utterly brilliant those  of you who watch my channel often enough  know that I'm not always this positive  about the works that I watch or read but  there is a reason I am now this show  delivers on every possible front the  story animation music sound design  compositing editing storyboarding  everything is working in tandem to bring  you this wonderful story and characters  in the best way it possibly can and the  story that we do get in the end is 100  worth that Herculean effort I have  watched a lot of anime and read a lot of  manga for this channel as well as in my  personal time across my whole life some  I've liked some not so much but it has  been quite some time since I so deeply  enjoyed watching an anime like this the  characters and themes it delivers are  remarkably genuine thoughtful and  enthralling and I can't wait for what  season two has in store for me  in the end the core motivation behind my  wanting to explore this series in  Greater detail was that I wanted to try  to make sense of why or how someone like  one became successful as a mangaka over  the years in reviewing these stories  from the East Miami has been to uncover  the footprints or fingerprints each and  every artist invariably leaves on their  work as I read them whether it be the  rebellious nature of Iraqi in JoJo's  Bizarre Adventure the pain and anguish  left behind by Togashi and hunter hunter  or even the initially sad but  inspirational journey of Kishimoto  through the likes of his Naruto series  normally people tend to have a  superficial reaction to one's work  because of how it looks on the surface  more so than any other successful  mangaka out there one's work tends to be  initially dismissed with those that are  not open to understanding how it reads  or how his work Works making up a common  part of one's experience trying to make  it as an artist in this industry however  true to the lessons he's learned and  almost exactly like the stories he's  written the crude looking mangas and the  silly stories he presents often have far  more going on right beneath the surface  than one might expect but once you do  notice it that's the moment that one not  only wins you over as a fan but  potentially if you're lucky changes your  outlook and approach to life for the  better and so before I finish this  episode I'd like to share a quote with  you nearing the end of a particular  conversation an interviewer says what he  takes away from Mob psycho 100 is that  you can truly grow up without  interacting with other people further  adding that he doesn't recall any other  manga that puts so much care into  depicting one's own personal growth in  response to these observations one  explains his approach towards mob psycho  100. what I have in mind is to tell a  big story of one little step I don't  believe our lives change completely for  the better at a short notice it's all  the small progress we make that's  important that's what I think while  drawing this manga  [Music]
 

